operty across from the house is  the former barn  during the socialist era the large  building served as a garage for farm  machines today it houses much of the  kafka's art collection  we wanted to let these rooms shine in a  new way  so we filled the space with artworks  that we love each one of which shines in  its own way  right next to the barn is the old hen  house nowadays babette kafka creates her  own pieces here  she specializes in relief-like textures  mounted on used wooden panels  this is my studio this is where i work  and spend as much time as possible  making art  i use different materials like coffee  grounds or sand to give the pictures a  certain materiality  so now where once cows were milked and  pigs were fattened this family has found  a place they can live with their art
 

